NG_CACHE` to a safe absolute","-directory. Payload or cleanup-helper integrity failures never trigger the","-profile retry.","-Under either persistent root, entries live in `swc-native-<effective UID or user","+it retries `%USERPROFILE%\\.swc-cache`, then `%ProgramData%`, for cache errors","+only, including in mode `0` and after a custom root fails. All three paths","+must be absolute and pass the same ownership, ACL, and reparse-point checks.","+The shared application-data root holds the existing protected","+`swc-native-<user SID>/v1` namespace. LocalAppData and the profile may grant","+another account replacement rights; the shared fallback preserves validation","+without changing either root's ACL. A usable cache does not consult later","+candidates. If no candidate is safe and writable, the error includes all three","+causes and recommends setting `SWC_NATIVE_BINDING_CACHE` to a safe absolute","+directory. Payload or cleanup-helper integrity failures never trigger another","+cache candidate.","+Under every persistent root, entries live in `swc-native-<effective UID or user"," SID>/v1/<128 hexadecimal SHA-512 digits>.node`. Unix directories are owner-only;"," Windows directories have protected owner/SYSTEM DACLs. Ancestor directories"," may also belong to Administrators or TrustedInstaller. Effective untrusted"],"additions":12,"deletions":10,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/swc_native_addon/src/cache.rs","lines":["@@ -124,34 +124,49 @@ pub fn cache_directory(root: &Path) -> Result<PathBuf> {","     Ok(version)"," }"," ","-/// Try the usual user cache first, then the platform fallback. Shared ancestors","-/// can make Unix home directories unsafe, as can ordinary Windows LocalAppData","-/// ACLs. Retry only cache failures, never payload corruption, and validate both","-/// roots using the same security checks. Primary success does no extra work.","+/// Try the usual user cache first, then the platform fallback. Windows also","+/// tries ProgramData when both profile roots fail. Retry only cache failures,","+/// never payload corruption, and validate every root with the same security","+/// checks. Primary success does no extra work."," fn with_user_cache_root<T>(materialize: impl Fn(&Path) -> Result<T>) -> Result<T> {","-    let primary = platform::user_cache_root().and_then(|root| materialize(&root));","-    if let Err(primary) = primary {","-        if primary.kind != ErrorKind::Cache {","-            return Err(primary);","-        }","-        tracing::debug!(error = %primary, \"native user cache unavailable; trying fallback cache\");","-        return platform::fallback_cache_root()","-            .and_then(|root| materialize(&root))","-            .map_err(|fallback| {","-                if fallback.kind != ErrorKind::Cache {","-                    return fallback;","-                }","-                Error::new(","-                    ErrorKind::Cache,","-                    format!(","-                        \"user cache failed: {primary}; fallback cache failed: {fallback}; set \\","-                         SWC_NATIVE_BINDING_CACHE to a safe absolute directory owned by your user \\","-                         whose ancestors do not grant other users replacement rights\"","-                    ),","-                )","-            });","+    let primary = match platform::user_cache_root().and_then(|root| materialize(&root)) {","+        Ok(value) => return Ok(value),","+        Err(error) if error.kind == ErrorKind::Cache => error,","+        Err(error) => return Err(error),","+    };","+    tracing::debug!(error = %primary, \"native user cache unavailable; trying fallback cache\");","+    let fallback = match platform::fallback_cache_root().and_then(|root| materialize(&root)) {","+        Ok(value) => return Ok(value),","+        Err(error) if error.kind == ErrorKind::Cache => error,","+        Err(error) => return Err(error),","+    };","+    #[cfg(windows)]","+    {","+        tracing::debug!(error = %fallback, \"native profile cache unavailable; trying shared cache\");","+        let shared = match platform::shared_cache_root().and_then(|root| materialize(&root)) {","+            Ok(value) => return Ok(value),","+            Err(error) if error.kind == ErrorKind::Cache => error,","+            Err(error) => return Err(error),","+        };","+        return Err(Error::new(","+            ErrorKind::Cache,","+            format!(","+                \"user cache failed: {primary}; fallback cache failed: {fallback}; ProgramData \\","+                 cache failed: {shared}; set SWC_NATIVE_BINDING_CACHE to a safe absolute \\","+                 directory owned by your user whose ancestors do not grant other users \\","+                 replacement rights\"","+            ),","+        ));","     }","-    primary","+    #[cfg(unix)]","+    Err(Error::new(","+        ErrorKind::Cache,","+        format!(","+            \"user cache failed: {primary}; fallback cache failed: {fallback}; set \\","+             SWC_NATIVE_BINDING_CACHE to a safe absolute directory owned by your user whose \\","+             ancestors do not grant other users replacement rights\"","+        ),","+    ))"," }"," "," pub fn materialize(payload: &Payload<'_>, mode: &CacheMode) -> Result<Materialized> {","@@ -160,9 +175,12 @@ pub fn materialize(payload: &Payload<'_>, mode: &CacheMode) -> Result<Materializ","         CacheMode::Default => with_user_cache_root(|root| cached_at(payload, root)),","         CacheMode::Custom(root) => match cached_at(payload, root) {","             Ok(file) => Ok(file),","-            Err(custom) => {","+            Err(custom) if custom.kind == ErrorKind::Cache => {","                 tracing::debug!(path = %root.display(), error = %custom, \"custom native cache unavailable; using user cache\");","                 with_user_cache_root(|root| cached_at(payload, root)).map_err(|default| {","+                    if default.kind != ErrorKind::Cache {","+                   